# Established Way of Working & Repository Guidelines

## 1. Deep Planning Mode & Issue Creation First
- **Core Rule**: All work MUST begin by creating a `did` issue (`did add refine/<issue>/issue.md`).
- **Zero Doubt Requirement**: Before writing code or modifying plans, perform exploratory research and ask clarifying questions.

## 2. Filesystem-Native Issue Lifecycle (`.did/`)
- **Directory Hierarchy Standard**: Directly under `.did/`, ONLY `implement`, `refine`, and `wont` (plus reserved `.hooks`) exist.
- **Staging in `.did/refine/`**: Unrefined or open proposals stay in `.did/refine/`.
- **Promotion to `.did/implement/`**: Move issues to `.did/implement/` only when 100% ready with explicit requirements and test plans.
- **Demotion Back to `.did/refine/` on Vagueness**: If any issue in `implement/` contains open questions, move it back to `refine/`.
- **Documenting Rejected Proposals in `.did/wont/`**: Document rejected proposals inside `.did/wont/<PROPOSAL>/issue.md`.

## 3. Hook Directory Sanctity (`.hooks/`)
- `.hooks/` directories inside `.did/` subtrees are strictly reserved for hook files (`show`, `status`, `done`, `add`, `link`, `mv`).

## 4. Testing & Verification Commands
- Run tests: `cargo test`
- Linting: `cargo clippy -- -D warnings`
- Code coverage check: `cargo llvm-cov --fail-under-lines 85`
